@startmindmap r-03-test-taxonomy
title Test taxonomy — what each layer is actually for

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam shadowing false

* Tests
** Unit  (-short)
*** No network, no Docker, no Keycloak
*** Every remote seam has a hostile fake
*** Runs in seconds, on save
** Contract  (-short)
*** One table per interface
*** Run against every implementation
*** Executor  local · ssh · docker · k8s
*** BlobStore  disk · sftp · s3 · azure
*** Catches "works on disk, differs on S3"
** Integration  (-tags=integration)
*** Keycloak fixture matrix
**** minimal · rich · federated
**** large (120k users) · legacy · themed
*** MinIO · Azurite · sshd · kind
*** The only place fidelity is provable
** Fault injection
*** Proxy that drops, stalls, truncates, corrupts
*** Resume across an app restart
*** Never produce a bundle that looks valid
** Do no harm
*** Serving workload untouched
*** The label trap
*** Teardown on all five exit paths
*** End-of-run leak sweep
** Redaction  (own CI stage)
*** Property test over the whole pipeline
*** Logs · audit · events · exports · sidecars
*** Over-redaction is a bug too
** Manual
*** Per phase, scripted, recorded
*** "Does this error help me?"
*** "Is it obvious this bundle is unencrypted?"

@endmindmap
